{
  "about": "Dry-end reject reasons as category -> reason, with position as attributes, never as reasons (issue #100). A reject line carries one category key, one reason of that category, and optionally a liner and a side from the lists the reason allows. `controllable` is who can act on it: yes (the corrugator crew), partly (receiving and roll prep), no, or unstated (the owner did not say). `counted_as` decides where the area is reported: dry_end lines are dry-end quality waste; changeover lines are counted with shear and sequencing, not dry-end quality; excluded lines are planning or administration, not production waste, reported separately. The demo generator emits only the bond, warp, misalignment and cracking categories (records.GENERATED_REJECT_CATEGORIES); the rest are the plant's list, kept so a record carrying them is classified, not guessed.",
